Notes:
1) The sensor on the top is supposed to be a MakerHawk piezo sensor. Since that component is not available in my diagramming software (Fritzing),
it is represented here using a generic piezo buzzer part for illustration purposes only. The sensor in the actual project (real photos) is used for detecting
vibration, not producing sound unlike the one on the bottom.

2) Tapping the sensor instead of strumming on guitar in the video for easier recording. When taped on to guitar, just use serial plotter to ensure the buzzer 
does not reach the threshold but the strums do.
